<title>PORTUGAL: Lisnave shareholders approve revamp.</title>
<headline>Lisnave shareholders approve revamp.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Portugal's loss-making Lisnave, one of Europe's biggest ship repairers, on Monday approved a rescue plan that would break the company up into three entities and writedown capital.</p>
<p>German group Thyssen Werften will become a partner in the ship repairing company. The government will be the major stakeholder in a human resources company which will absorb excess Lisnave labour, while a third concern will take over management of the group's infrastructure.</p>
<p>Capital was cut tenfold to 3.56 billion escudos.</p>
<p>Lisnave posted a 5.54 billion escudo loss for 1996 on Monday, down from 9.59 billion the previous year.</p>
<p>($1=170.76 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
